\mathrm{Na}_2 \mathrm{CO}_3+\mathrm{HCl} \longrightarrow \mathrm{NaHCO}_3+\mathrm{NaCl}

The remaining solution then contains the unreacted $\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$ from this reaction plus the unreacted $\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$ originally in the solution. At the phenolphthalein end point, there is no reaction between $\mathrm{HCl}$ and $\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$.
